    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Using the binomial theorem, the expansion of $(x+y)^6$ is given by:\n$$(x+y)^6 = \\binom{6}{0}x^6y^0 + \\binom{6}{1}x^5y^1 + \\binom{6}{2}x^4y^2 + \\binom{6}{3}x^3y^3 + \\binom{6}{4}x^2y^4 + \\binom{6}{5}x^1y^5 + \\binom{6}{6}x^0y^6$$\n\nThe problem asks for the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term, so we need to look for the term with $x^2y^4$ in the expansion.\n\nBy comparing the terms in the expansion, we see that the term with $x^2y^4$ is $\\binom{6}{4}x^2y^4$.\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of the $x^2y^4$ term is $\\boxed{\\binom{6}{4}}$.",
